    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": {
        "en": "Liaison: How to Carry the Sound Over",
        "ko": "소리 나는 대로 읽는 연음 법칙"
      },
      "text": "When a syllable ending with a batchim is followed by a syllable starting with the silent vowel placeholder ㅇ, move the final consonant sound directly into that vowel: 물 + 이 → [무리], 밥 + 을 → [바블], 옷 + 이 → [오시]. If a consonant follows, pronounce the representative sound: 옷장 → [옫짱]."
    },
